  message: "Fixed in PR #1320 (merged, dev d48540acc7). catalog_provenance gains 'tiers': every file the verify-claims run read, under builtin/community/yours/in_repo (git state for a file inside the repo), plus completeness grants from config.toml / io_primitives.d / opted-in .hypergumbo.toml (origin user_channel/config/in_repo_config) and withheld_completeness_grants for community files; user_supplied true when any yours/in_repo file loaded. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE on merged dev: a run with a config.toml io_primitives path and an init-catalogs-seeded home -> tiers.yours [mine.yaml], tiers.community [the 8 seeded overlays + shipped community taint/summary/overlay files], tiers.builtin [python.yaml, taint + summary built-ins], user_supplied true (the filed case read user_supplied false with no layer). Statement scope NOT fully asserted: the shipped files of the analysis-stage families (frameworks, dataflow_patterns, library_signatures, cfg_nodes, url_folding) are not listed (the graph does not record which the analysis consulted) -- filed as a residual. Also noted: io overlays for OTHER languages (seeded elixir/go/...) are listed because they are read and parsed, though their rows apply to no language in the run."  # c9af
